592186045417 true] [17592186417210 1077 "field-1" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417210 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417205 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417210 1079 #uuid "f131aa45-b457-59cb-b20c-8d7c35137875" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417207 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1069 "q-335653" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{3}(t)+y(t)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1072 #uuid "307f17c8-f71c-5dc2-a87d-04fc684fa18f" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true] [17592186417211 1074 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y+1=0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+y+1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+1=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+y+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+(-x-1)+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}-x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ x(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\text{ }0,\\text{ }1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $y:$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=-0-1=-1.$\n\n- For $x=1,$ we get $y=-1-1=-2.$\n\n- For $x=-1,$ we get $y=-(-1)-1=0.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\text{and}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534280 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00e92b02-6a9b-5d57-8c16-a54ee1f5ab06" 17592186417193 "answer-091b64ac-c431-5b8f-af2d-93c9caba880c" 17592186417194 "answer-1115c611-afc1-502d-b2ee-dd7d365f08c6" 175921